																		Music makes you lose control - Declass attempt
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/coelacanthcanon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6620369); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6620369&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609362898" alt="CoelacanthCanon" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6620369)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/coelacanthcanon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6620369); return false;" >CoelacanthCanon</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609314493 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Dec 2020 07:48</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4857157">
									

<p>The article is well written, but I find the narrative hard to understand. I think an official declassification would be very good.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Attempt&nbsp;at&nbsp;D-class-if-cation</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Probably&nbsp;wrong&nbsp;in&nbsp;some&nbsp;places</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The red portions of the article indicate a change from the original article. Let's look at the original text first.</p>
<p>Originally, two personnel talk about the technology and how SCP-3955 is recorded. By putting a music creating AI in a <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">WARP Train from Library of Ruina</span> box that accelerates time, SCP-3955 will be observed in the created music. A few examples are provided, and the article ends.</p>
<p>Except for the mysterious edits that have been placed in the article. SCP-3955 doesn't need to be contained or concealment, but its now an Apollyon class SCP. Whoever is editing this article doesn't want the anomaly to be referred as an SCP. Re-reading the article, it seems like ██████ ████ (one of the scientists behind the anomaly) is trying to stop a rogue AI (the AI being tested to make music) from changing the document.</p>
<p>██████ ████ has a portion of their text in the Conprocs, as there's a note that unauthorized changes are to be reverted immediately. To me, this edit in the Conprocs is very different from the other edits. Potentially, they might be losing control of the entire article in addendum 03. This addendum was made when the article was last updated, and the editor's words begin to become heavily blackboxed. Quote:</p>
<p>&quot;On April 12th, at 4:02&#160;pm, Dr. ████ followed up on a hunch regarding ███-3955's possible connections to a series of abstract, deep-space transmissions found in CRYSTAL-INE's database. Findings indicate ████ ██ ███ ██ █████ █████ ██████ ██ ████ ███ ███ ████ █████████ ██████ ███ █████ ██ █ ████ ██ █████.</p>
<p>There are to be no further additions to this document.&quot;</p>
<p>Once the AI takes control of the article, it starts heavily blackboxing everything related to the SCP Foundation. The reason for this is that the AI has gained some sentience. This is evident in addendum 04, where the AI begins to feel emotion and develops advanced thoughts. At first, it has its basic functions listed and it begins to become wary of its purpose. It starts going insane and starts questioning music, even giving names to its &quot;cyclical&quot; music processes. Once the AI finds the document, it tries to change it dramatically, even putting a warning in the Conprocs to stop testing. Due to its lack of access privileges, the article remains in its editing phase.</p>
<p>&#8230;Re-reading this, the rogue AI thin is probably all incorrect. It's just strange that edits are being made after 16:02, as addendum 04 has a log from 16:04. If this really is an Apollyon, is it talking about how music is unstoppable? Or did the AI find out that SCP-3955 is very dangerous for humans?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Probably wasted time writing that, but eh. +1</p>

